      "contentRewrites": {
        "win32:overview": {
          "Load `cpp` first, then `win32:knowledge` for calibration and\n`win32:style` when writing Windows API glue. Language-version defaults remain in\n`cpp`. If the repository selects MSVC/clang-cl, also load `msvc:toolchain`; if it\nselects G++, load `gpp:toolchain` instead.": "Load `base` first, then `win32:knowledge` for calibration and\n`win32:style` when writing Windows API glue. Language-version defaults remain in\n`base`. This legacy combined package supplies `msvc:toolchain`; migrate to the\nexplicit `gpp` plus `win32` split before selecting G++ for Win32 work."
        },
        "win32:style": {
          "- Compiler, ABI, runtime, build-system, and editor configuration belong to the selected\n  toolchain skill: `msvc:toolchain` or `gpp:toolchain`. The following settings\n  apply to the Win32 target independently of that choice.": "- This legacy combined package supplies `msvc:toolchain` for compiler, ABI, runtime,\n  build-system, and editor configuration. Migrate to the explicit split before pairing\n  Win32 with another toolchain. The following settings apply to the Win32 target."
